  "body": "**Replaces #271**, which closed itself on 2026-11-10 when its branch was pushed: the old fork `austin62jake/Camcraft` had left this repo's fork network, so GitHub could no longer follow its head. Same commits, now from the new fork `austin62jake/Camcraft2`, with `main` f42d3788 merged in (no conflicts). The review history and mkinney's conflict notes are on #271.\n\nFork: `austin62jake/Camcraft2`, created 2026-11-10 from upstream `main` f42d3788 (contains v0.16.0, PROCESS_VERSION 4).\n\n**Partial fix for #266.** This removes one of the two checks that refuse a tap on a normally modelled hole. The other one still blocks the post; see \"What is left\" below.\n\n### What changed\n\n- The program sim (the stock-sim clause of the post gate) swept a Tap-kind tool at its full major diameter. CAD models a tapped hole at the thread's minor (tap-drill) size, and a tap only cuts the thread band outside that wall. So the sim read the band as a gouge down the whole hole wall and refused the post.\n- A Tap-kind tool now sweeps its thread's core: `diameter / 2 - 0.5413 x pitch`. That is the ISO 724 radial thread depth, the same constant the thread-mill generator already uses (`machining2d::THREAD_DEPTH_PER_PITCH`). For M6 x 1 the core is Ø4.917.\n- The rule lives in one place, `operation::tool_law::cutting_radius`, so a later fix to the generator's verify can read the same number. Every other tool still sweeps half its diameter. A pitch too coarse to leave a core is refused by name.\n- A tap over a hole smaller than its core, or over solid metal, is still a gouge.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/266-tap-minor-sweep.md`.\n\n### Readings\n\n| Case (M6 x 1 tap, plate with a blind hole) | Program sim before | Program sim after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ø5 hole (tap drill) | gouge, worst 12.000 mm on the hole wall | clean, 0 gouge cells |\n| Ø3 hole (too small) | gouge | gouge (still refused) |\n\n### Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/tap_sim.rs`)\n\n- `a_tap_in_a_hole_modelled_at_tap_drill_size_is_not_a_gouge`: fails on `main` (`worst 12.000 mm at (-0.31, -2.94, z 8.0)`), passes with the fix.\n- `a_tap_wider_than_its_hole_is_still_a_gouge`: guards the other side; passes before and after.\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local)\n\n**On this head (9410e5ba, `main` f42d3788 merged), Windows 10:**\n\n- The quick gate's plan (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -DryRun`, run by hand at `-j 4`): app lib 103 passed, plus 24 suites, 130 passed: `carried_fixtures_cache` 6, `carried_verify` 8, `contour_arc_sim` 1, `edge_break_bound` 3, `edge_break_gate` 5, `lathe_field_sim` 6, `lathe_field_tools` 2, `post_not_judged` 4, `posting` 17, `probe_only_sim` 2, `real_tip_contour` 4, `rotary_field_parity` 3, `setup_align` 9, `setup_carry` 9, `setup_stock_source` 6, `stock_engine_agreement` 0, `stock_export` 2, `stock_field_cost` 0, `stock_sim_document` 9, `stock_view` 4, `tap_sim` 2, `tool_law` 4, `verify` 21, `wall_column_gouge` 3. 7 are `#[ignore]`d in the source (`rotary_field_parity` 1, `stock_engine_agreement` 3, `stock_field_cost` 1, `verify` 2). No failures.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n**On the earlier heads (#271):**\n\n\n- Both pinning tests alone, with the fix, and with `stock_sim.rs` put back to `main` (the first one fails there as above).\n- `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick`: app lib plus 13 suites (the gate map's `stock_sim` and `tool_law` suites plus `tap_sim`), 155 tests, all pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The app, through `camcraft-cli mcp`, built from this branch (upstream `main` 897a820 plus this commit): imported a plate STL with a round Ø5 blind hole, added `TAP-M6` and a Drill/Tap op, generated, verified. The program gate now reports `ok` with no problems. With a Ø3 hole it still reports `gouge: program cuts below the model in 127 cell(s), worst 6.00 mm`.\n- Baseline batch tier on clean `main` 897a820 on this machine: all suites pass except three UI pixel snapshots (`egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light`, `tool_editor_snapshot`), which also fail without this change. Not run on Linux or macOS.\n\n### What is left (why this is `Refs`, not `Fixes`)\n\nWith this fix the Ø5 tap job still does not post. The op's own verify flags `move 1 cuts past the finish surface` and `move 2 cuts past the finish surface` (the tap feeding in and out). That verify hands one tool radius (`tool.geom()`) to every law, including the rapids laws, where a tap's full diameter is the right envelope: a tap must never rapid into the thread band. I tried shrinking only the containment solid law's cutter; the tangency law still flags the same two moves, so I dropped that. Fixing it means splitting the cutting radius from the rapid envelope in the verifier's inputs, and it meets the convention in `solid_law_goldens.rs` that a tapped hole is modelled at the tap's major diameter. I left that for you to decide on the issue.\n\nChangelog: The program sim no longer reads a tap's thread band as a gouge on a hole modelled at tap-drill size (#266, partial)\n\nRefs #266\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
